{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "ssvc_a26",
  "notes": "Fresh isolated state. Enters the alphanumeric Switch Test from attract mode: one press of the toggled Green service button (DE_COMPORTS), then Black presses until the title SWITCH TEST is shown. The service buttons are the only keyboard inputs; every probe is a direct write to a public matrix address no DE_COMPORTS key backs, and the driver has no simData. The sweep covers public 9-64 except 30 and 31, the FLIP3031 pair core_updateSw rewrites from the cabinet flipper buttons. Each probe holds one public address at 1 for 3 s, preceded by a 3 s reference closure of public 17 (public 9 when the probed address is 17). On the pinned 97aa922b build the Switch Test keeps the last name on screen after release, so a release frame proves nothing: a probe whose held reading differs from the reference reading before it was printed for the probed address, and a probe that repeats the reference reading has no name of its own. On that build the displayed segments change gradually: a 2 s hold once caught a frame blending the previous name with the new one, so each hold is 3 s.",
